Apple today announced that it has rebuilt the search infrastructure that powers key features like Spotlight, <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/guide/photos/">Photos</a>, and Mail across all of its major next-generation software platforms.<br/>
<br/>
<img src="https://images.macrumors.com/article-new/2026/02/ios-26-4-apple-games-search.jpg" alt="" width="2000" height="1125" class="aligncenter size-full wp-image-1037221" /><br/>
The company says the index has been rearchitected to be more stable, efficient, and comprehensive, covering both old and new content. After updating, the new infrastructure will begin reindexing device content automatically.<br/>
<br/>
